From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 19:56:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Music suite: built-in CC library + AI-composed beds for
 videos
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Solves "I don't have a music file" — the background-music section now has
three paths instead of one:

1. Upload (unchanged).
2. Library: lib/musicLibrary.ts searches Openverse (the Creative-Commons
   aggregator over Jamendo/Freesound/Wikimedia) filtered to
   commercially-usable licenses; license + attribution travel with every
   result. GET /ai/music/search returns tracks with in-dialog audio preview;
   POST /ai/music/import downloads the pick server-side (https-only,
   public-host SSRF guard re-checked per redirect hop, 15 MB cap) into
   tenant storage and returns a normal musicPath. No API key needed.
3. AI compose: describe a mood ("warm lofi chill beat") and
   videoGen/musicGen.ts generates an instrumental bed via Replicate
   MusicGen (meta/musicgen) using the SAME Replicate token the video engine
   already has — no new secrets. Beds are steered instrumental/loopable;
   MusicGen's 30s ceiling is fine because both composers loop the bed with
   a fade. Priced at +1 video unit (reserved up front, refunded on failure,
   ignored when an uploaded track wins). Job progress shows "Composing the
   music".

Contract: musicPrompt on generate-video, /ai/music/search + /ai/music/import
paths, MusicTrack/MusicSearchResults/LibraryMusicImportResult schemas.

Verified: 80 videoGen tests green (musicGen create/poll/download, clamping,
not-configured), musicLibrary SSRF + parsing suite, 34 route tests incl.
import round-trip and +1-unit funding, 13 studio page tests, root typecheck,
spec lint, codegen committed. No schema change.

